#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0376 expect=skipped domain=ADLBC
#note "DISCRIMINATOR of the R-5.25 split, on the byte-identical dataset of the sibling's violation fixture: APERIODC is present-and-blank while the primary APERIOD is populated - the *C state, owned by PMDA-AD0376-A. This parent owns only the *N arm, and the dataset carries NO *N candidate at all, so the wildcard expansion set is empty -> NoMatch -> SKIPPED (the same mechanism as -skipped_excluded_secondary). The sibling's state is never reported by this rule, which is the point."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLBC
col STUDYID  type=Char
col USUBJID  type=Char
col PARAMCD  type=Char
col APERIOD  type=Num
col APERIODC type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALB | 1 |
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1023 | ALB | 2 | PERIOD2
